    Re-fetch the VM secret userdata if it was changed

commit 73b73d19bb90207f18a408e97153fa1cb6faa12c
Author: Roy Golan <rgolan@redhat.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 28 15:04:03 2022 +0200

    Rebuild the cloud-init userdata if the soure VM secret changed
    
    After 24 hours the userdata secret for a VM contains an outdated value.
    
    We must refetch and update the cloud init secret with the latest data,
    otherwise a node will fail the ignition stage.
    
    Signed-off-by: Roy Golan <rgolan@redhat.com>

commit 68ebbe0177b06bdace731b4149976f907419763c
Merge: 1c6ec37 0861f72
Author: Kubernetes Prow Robot <k8s-ci-robot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Mar 7 13:56:34 2023 -0800

    Merge pull request #226 from jmhbnz/main
    
    Replace deprecated k8s registry references

commit 0861f72f2a01dfc447c1678e66ef2ff99c73cb1e
Author: James Blair <mail@jamesblair.net>
Date:   Sat Feb 25 09:24:09 2023 +1300

    Replace deprecated k8s registry references
    
    Problem: Previously all of Kubernetes' image hosting has been out of gcr.io. There were significant egress costs associated with this when images were pulled from entities outside gcp. Refer to https://github.com/kubernetes/k8s.io/wiki/New-Registry-url-for-Kubernetes-(registry.k8s.io)
    
    Solution: As highlighted at KubeCon NA 2022 k8s infra SIG update, the replacement for k8s.gcr.io which is registry.k8s.io is now ready for mainstream use and the old k8s.gcr.io has been formally deprecated and projects are requested to migrate off it. This commit migrates remaining references for kubernetes-sigs/cluster-api-provider-kubevirt to registry.k8s.io.
    Signed-off-by: James Blair <mail@jamesblair.net>

commit 1c6ec370122d9f0b454d5ca89819d3c2ee8fe728
Merge: 54ac76b c5ff039
Author: Kubernetes Prow Robot <k8s-ci-robot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Feb 15 09:42:33 2023 -0800

    Merge pull request #225 from nunnatsa/improve-linter
    
    Add the ginkgolinter and fix findings

commit c5ff0395e08e9f726412c3403ecb9c1d33d43d2b
Author: Nahshon Unna-Tsameret <nunnatsa@redhat.com>
Date:   Tue Feb 14 07:16:12 2023 +0200

    Add the ginkgolinter and fix findings
    
    In addition to the ginkgo linter findings, replace this pattern:
    ```go
    err = funcRetErr()
    Expect(err).ToNot(HaveOccurred())
    ```
    
    With the more readable version of:
    ```go
    Expect(funcRetErr()).To(Succeed())
    ```
    
    Improve some Eventually usages by using the Gomega parameter instead of returning error, to get cleaner test code.
    
    Also, replaced some deprecation methods.
    
    Signed-off-by: Nahshon Unna-Tsameret <nunnatsa@redhat.com>

