commit 5ff4ba0cf9eac83901a0340756f923d079e9c473
Author: Radim Hrazdil <rhrazdil@redhat.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 5 12:52:16 2022 +0200

    e2e, conformance: introduce conformance tests
    
    Conformance tests are executed with sonobuoy, which
    run from a pod deployed in infra cluster.
    
    The conformance e2e tests themselve are running in
    the tenant cluster.
    The pod mounts the tenant cluster kubeconfig
    from the <cluster-name>-kubeconfig secret.
    
    The run-conformance.sh script creates a configMap
    with names of tests that need to be skipped due to
    issues with DNS (accessing services via internal
    domain name) in the guest cluster.
    
    Signed-off-by: Radim Hrazdil <rhrazdil@redhat.com>

